A||||5||Ironhorse||Belt for 3.8||||1||
Z||000000||Ironhorse||06-11-2001||09:19 PM||||I have a 86 olds Delta 88 3.8 engine that's been rebuilt with only 500 miles on it.  I'm slowly working on putting it in F-15.  The thing I'm concern is that when I remove the AC and the steering pump, I don't see how I can hook up the belt using Gates K060640 belt.  Would I still need to use the tension pulley?  Thanks in advance for time and wisdom.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ironhorse||06-12-2001||03:27 PM||||C'on ain't there no love in this place anymore?||||reg||1
Z||000002||elfiero||06-12-2001||04:02 PM||||We love ya man!<BR>Heres what you do,remove the P/S pump,A/C<BR>comp,and the idler pully(LH thds)go get a<BR>idler pulley from a 302 EFI ford and install<BR>in stock position.This is grooved instead of<BR>smooth so the belt will track and not wear <BR>on the inside.Now,slice your old belt and<BR>install it around your alt,waterpump,crank<BR>pully and idler.have a friend take a wrench<BR>and crank the tensioner to its full travel<BR>now,mark the overlap on the belt and remove.<BR>lay it on the floor and measure it for length<BR>now go to NAPA with this measurement and tell<BR>the counter PERSON you need a six rib belt<BR>that length.Take this new belt home and install it!Problem solved.<BR>P.S.make sure you go the correct direction<BR>around the waterpump.Have fun!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000003||Ironhorse||06-12-2001||06:17 PM||||*cheesy joyous dancing among the forums* I'm feelin da luvvvvvvvv.  Anyway, Thanks for the info.  One more thing, what year ford 302?||||reg||12
Z||000004||Ironhorse||06-13-2001||10:01 PM||||BUMP||||reg||5
Z||000005||elfiero||06-13-2001||10:30 PM||||89-92 EFI 302 from just about all the body styles.||||reg||6
